// @error-at 17:11 i32[] is not f64[]: this join would hold both, and a container never widens implicitly. Its elements would be stored differently, so it would be a copy, and a write through either list would not reach the other. Build it as `f64[]`, or copy it with `.map((x) => x as f64)`
// @error-at 20:20 f32[] is not f64[]: this join would hold both, and a container never widens implicitly
// @error-at 24:7 i32[] is not f64[]: this join would hold both, and a container never widens implicitly
